.TH CONTAINER-EXPLORER 1 "" "container-explorer" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
container-explorer \- offline forensic explorer for container runtimes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B container-explorer
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fICOMMAND OPTIONS\fR] [\fIARGUMENTS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B container-explorer
explores, analyzes, and performs digital forensics on containerd, Docker, and
Podman storage directories offline without running container daemons.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable debug log messages.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-image\-root " " \fIPATH\fR
Mount point for an offline disk image.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-containerd\-root " " \fIPATH\fR
Containerd root directory.
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-docker\-root " " \fIPATH\fR
Docker root directory.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-use\-layer\-cache
Use cached layers where layers are symlinks.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-layer\-cache " " \fINAME\fR
Cached layer folder within the snapshot root (default: \fBlayers\fR).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-support\-container\-data " " \fIFILE\fR
YAML file listing Kubernetes support container rules (for example,
\fI/etc/container-explorer/supportcontainer.yaml\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-output " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format: \fBtable\fR (default) or \fBjson\fR.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Write output to the given file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help text.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version information.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR list " (" ls ")"
List \fBnamespaces\fR, \fBcontainers\fR, \fBimages\fR, \fBcontents\fR,
\fBsnapshots\fR, or \fBtasks\fR.
.TP
.BR info ", " inspect
Display container metadata and OCI runtime specifications.
.TP
.BR mount
Mount a container's merged filesystem to a target directory.
.TP
.BR drift " (" diff ")"
Report added, modified, and newly introduced executable files relative to the
base image.
.TP
.BR export
Export a container filesystem as a raw ext4 image (\fB.raw\fR) or gzipped tar
archive (\fB.tar.gz\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/container-explorer/supportcontainer.yaml
Packaged Kubernetes support container criteria file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
sudo container-explorer \-\-image-root /mnt/disk1 list containers
.br
sudo container-explorer \-\-image-root /mnt/disk1 \-\-output json drift <id>
.br
sudo container-explorer \-\-image-root /mnt/disk1 export \-a <id> /tmp/exports/
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
Upstream documentation at https://github.com/google/container-explorer.
